WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.644 --> 00:00:03.426
- [Narrator] In the United
Kingdom pies are king.

00:00:03.426 --> 00:00:04.411
Not just for the cherries

00:00:04.411 --> 00:00:06.829
and the apples that you Yanks are used to,

00:00:06.829 --> 00:00:07.912
you have your chicken,

00:00:07.912 --> 00:00:10.775
your steak and kidney, your pork pie,

00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:14.059
and in one tiny fishing
town, you have this:

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:16.017
a pie with, what?

00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:18.184
Wait, is that a fish head?

00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:22.258
Eugh, you've gotta be kidding me.

00:00:24.113 --> 00:00:26.970
- Trust me, you're gonna love it.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.834
- [Narrator] In this tiny fishing village,

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.017
there's a pub,

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:31.146
and in that pub,

00:00:31.146 --> 00:00:33.414
they make stargazy pie.

00:00:33.414 --> 00:00:35.435
It's a tradition that legend has it,

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.988
has been happening here
for hundreds of years.

00:00:37.988 --> 00:00:40.238
Which begs the question, why?

00:00:40.238 --> 00:00:43.560
- The Stargazy pie
is a pie which celebrates

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.390
Tom Bawcock’s going out

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.096
and catching seven different kinds of fish

00:00:48.096 --> 00:00:50.096
on the 23rd of December.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.472
- [Narrator] You see,
according to the legend

00:00:53.472 --> 00:00:55.317
it'd been a stormy winter.

00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:58.089
This meant no boat
managed to go out and fish,

00:00:58.089 --> 00:00:59.820
so people were starving.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.951
But a local fisherman, Tom Bawcock,

00:01:01.951 --> 00:01:03.735
he wasn't going to let his people die.

00:01:03.735 --> 00:01:04.568
- [Tom] I'm going.

00:01:04.568 --> 00:01:05.783
- [Narrator] He went out through the gate,

00:01:05.783 --> 00:01:07.011
yes, that gate,

00:01:07.011 --> 00:01:09.562
and braved the storm and--

00:01:09.562 --> 00:01:12.223
- And caught the different kinds of fish

00:01:12.223 --> 00:01:13.461
and brought it back.

00:01:13.461 --> 00:01:15.255
He made the pie.

00:01:15.255 --> 00:01:16.973
- [Narrator] And that brings us to today.

00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:18.837
Tracy, take it away.

00:01:18.837 --> 00:01:21.157
- You get six different whitefish,

00:01:21.157 --> 00:01:24.496
bake that in the oven with
some herbs and some lemon zest,

00:01:24.496 --> 00:01:26.250
put a layer of grated eggs,

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.877
a nice mashed potato
with loads of cream in

00:01:28.877 --> 00:01:31.145
and then you put a pastry lid.

00:01:31.145 --> 00:01:32.921
Put pilchards, cut them,

00:01:32.921 --> 00:01:35.451
and then you put so that the
heads are coming out the pie

00:01:35.451 --> 00:01:37.304
and the tails are coming out the pie.

00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:41.464
You assemble all the stars round the pie.

00:01:41.464 --> 00:01:44.298
On the 23rd of December,
we give it away free

00:01:44.298 --> 00:01:47.302
to thousands of people
that come to the village

00:01:47.302 --> 00:01:49.768
to celebrate Tom Bawcock's Night.

00:01:49.768 --> 00:01:51.996
- [Narrator] So to Tom
Bawcock, what a legend.

00:01:51.996 --> 00:01:53.484
Cheers, Tom.

00:01:53.484 --> 00:01:55.101
So, shall we taste it?

00:01:55.101 --> 00:01:57.074
- Mm mm, that is good.

00:01:57.074 --> 00:01:58.041
- Delicious.

00:01:58.041 --> 00:01:59.968
That really is quite delicious.

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:01.114
- It's good.

00:02:01.114 --> 00:02:02.494
Really good.

00:02:02.494 --> 00:02:03.726
- The fish is lovely.

00:02:03.726 --> 00:02:05.245
- It's most interesting,

00:02:05.245 --> 00:02:08.469
it's much milder than I thought.

00:02:08.469 --> 00:02:09.719
Mmm, fish bone.

